// Practice quiz: async and await
// First draft: unreviewed. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: html-css-js/dom-tooling-and-async/async-and-await

::o1 equivalent code::getA() returns a promise, and you want the id of its result. Which code does this in an async function? {
~const a \= getA(); return a.id; #Not quite. Without await, a is the promise.
~await return getA().id; #Not quite. That is not valid syntax.
~return await a.id; #Not quite. a has not been declared.
=const a \= await getA(); return a.id; #Correct. await unwraps the value, and the return fulfils the promise of the async function.
}

::o2 where to await::A rejection should be caught by try and catch. Where must the await be? {
~After the catch block #Not quite. Then the try cannot see it.
~Before the function keyword #Not quite. That is the async keyword, not await.
~It does not matter #Not quite. A rejection outside the try is not caught.
=Inside the try block #Correct. That is where the rejection throws.
}

::o2 throwing::An async function throws an Error. What does the caller receive? {
~The exception, synchronously at the call #Not quite. It arrives through the promise.
=A promise that rejects with that Error #Correct. Throwing in an async function rejects its promise.
~undefined #Not quite. The function returned a promise.
~A fulfilled promise holding the Error #Not quite. A throw rejects, not fulfils.
}

::o3 return wraps::async function n() \{ return 5; \} What is n()? {
=A promise fulfilled with 5 #Correct. async functions always return promises.
~5 #Not quite. You need await or then to get the value.
~A function #Not quite. Calling it gave you its return.
~undefined #Not quite. A value was returned, wrapped in a promise.
}

::o3 await a non-promise::What does const x \= await 7; do inside an async function? {
~It throws a TypeError #Not quite. Awaiting a non-promise is allowed.
~x is a promise #Not quite. await unwraps it.
=x is 7, after a brief pause in that function #Correct. await wraps a non-promise value and continues later.
~x is undefined #Not quite. The value passes through.
}
